"""packs/social_sciences.py — the social sciences specialization pack.

Covers: Political Science, International Relations, Sociology, Psychology,
Social Work, Demography, Mass Communication, Journalism and Media Studies.

Every atom teaches real social science grounded in named scholarship: Weber's
authority types, Durkheim's anomie and solidarity, Marx's class analysis,
structural-functionalism versus conflict theory, Cooley, Mead and Goffman on
the self, socialisation agents, Merton's strain typology, two-step flow,
agenda setting, framing, uses and gratifications, the hypodermic needle
critique. Nigerian grounding throughout: the 1999 Constitution (supremacy in
section 1, Chapter II objectives, Chapter III citizenship in sections 25 to
32, Chapter IV rights in sections 33 to 46, section 162 Federation Account),
36 states plus the FCT, INEC and the Electoral Act 2022 with BVAS, EFCC and
ICPC, NHIA 2022, VAPP 2015, ACJA 2015, NAFDAC against fake product claims,
the Nigerian press from Iwe Iroyin 1859 to the digital newsroom, and the
Lagos megacity as a live laboratory of urban theory. All numeric quiz keys
were verified with executed Python arithmetic before being written.
"""

