        "Culture is the learned, shared design for living of a society: its language, values, norms, beliefs, artefacts and institutions. Norms are rules of behaviour, ranging from folkways such as greeting elders to mores whose violation invites strong sanction, and laws enforced by the state. Values are shared ideas about what is good and worth pursuing. Nigerian society blends ethnic traditions with religion and global influence, so {S} treats culture as learned and changing, never as biologically fixed.",
