        ("mcq", "Which sector contributes the largest share of Nigeria's GDP?",
         "Services", ["Oil", "Agriculture", "Solid minerals"],
         "Services lead GDP; oil leads exports; agriculture leads rural employment."),
        ("mcq", "Durkheim's term for solidarity based on interdependence of specialised roles is, in {S},",
         "organic solidarity", ["mechanical solidarity", "anomie", "collective conscience"],
         "Organic solidarity arises from the division of labour and mutual dependence."),
        ("mcq", "The informal economy in Nigeria is best described as",
         "largely unregistered small-scale activity employing most non-farm workers", ["criminal activity", "foreign firms only", "government parastatals"],
         "Informality is unregistered but lawful activity, and it dominates non-farm employment."),
        ("tf", "The Contributory Pension Scheme of 2004 replaced the old defined-benefit public pension system.",
         "True", ["False"],
         "The Pension Reform Act framework moved public service pensions to contributory accounts."),
        ("mcq", "The National Health Insurance Authority Act of 2022, used in {S} discussions of welfare,",
         "seeks to extend health coverage to more Nigerians through pooled mechanisms", ["privatises hospitals", "bans private clinics", "sets drug prices"],
         "NHIA 2022 makes insurance coverage mandatory and pools funds for the vulnerable."),
        ("mcq", "In Easton's phrase, the political system allocates",
         "values authoritatively for society", ["wages by seniority", "grades by ability", "seats by lottery"],
         "Easton defined politics as the authoritative allocation of values."),
